(Send signal 0 to a LIVE child pid sets no error flag. The parent forks,
 sends signal 0 to the child (which is alive and waiting), asserts via
 On error that no error was raised, then SIGKILLs and reaps so the test
 completes fast. The "unexpected error" line must NOT appear in the
 output - its absence is the proof that a successful kill(2) cleared
 _last_error.)

Set pid to fork the process.
If pid is 0 then,
    Wait 30 seconds.
If pid is greater than 0 then,
    Send signal 0 to process pid.
    On error print "unexpected error on live child".
    Send signal 9 to process pid.
    Set reaped to reap any child process.
    If reaped is pid then,
        Print "signal 0 ok then reaped".